l-0",{"children":["\n",["$","li","li-0",{"children":"Deterministic noise scoring using nearest-rank percentile algorithms"}],"\n",["$","li","li-1",{"children":"Incident & deployment correlation to suppress recommendations during real incidents"}],"\n",["$","li","li-2",{"children":"Surgical IaC discovery with exact line number pinpointing"}],"\n",["$","li","li-3",{"children":"Human approval gate architecture (no autonomous writes)"}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p","p-5",{"children":["$","$L13","a-0",{"href":"/docs/alert-ai-tuner","children":"Read Alert Fatigue Tuner documentation →"}]}],"\n",["$","h3","h3-1",{"id":"kubernetes-ai-responder","children":"Kubernetes AI Responder"}],"\n",["$","p","p-6",{"children":["The ",["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Kubernetes AI Responder"}]," plugin provides an automated diagnostic agent that investigates Kubernetes workload failures on-demand, triggered by Alertmanager webhooks or manual developer actions."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-7",{"children":["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Key Features:"}]}],"\n",["$","ul","ul-1",{"children":["\n",["$","li","li-0",{"children":"Deterministic failure classification for common K8s errors"}],"\n",["$","li","li-1",{"children":"Bounded log collection with memory safeguards"}],"\n",["$","li","li-2",{"children":"Citation-backed diagnostics separating observed data from inference"}],"\n",["$","li","li-3",{"children":"Multi-turn incident memory for follow-up troubleshooting"}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p","p-8",{"children":["$","$L13","a-0",{"href":"/docs/kubernetes-ai-responder","children":"Read Kubernetes AI Responder documentation →"}]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-1",{"id":"architecture-philosophy","children":"Architecture Philosophy"}],"\n",["$","p","p-9",{"children":"All incident response plugins share these architectural principles:"}],"\n",["$","ol","ol-0",{"children":["\n",["$","li","li-0",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Read-Only First"}],": Agents start with pure diagnostics before gaining m